    "explanation": "To the rider: your SGD 4.50 cancellation fee is refunded in full. To the driver: the fee does not stand and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nThe determining fact is where the vehicle actually was. EV-GPS-02709 (weight 1.0, 100% coverage, no gaps) puts the driver's closest approach to the pickup pin at 647.3 m, with zero qualifying in-geofence fixes and a longest qualifying in-geofence run of 0.0 s against the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius in fee_schedule.arrival_radius_m. POL-NS-02 deems a driver to have arrived only where the trace contains at least three consecutive in-radius fixes; there are none, so the driver never arrived and POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails. POL-NS-06 makes the fee non-chargeable on its own terms as well: the effective in-geofence dwell is 0.0 s against the 180 s free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec), a 180 s shortfall. POL-NS-03 cannot rescue the fee, because its wrong-entrance route reaches only a driver stationary outside the radius but within 400 m of the pin; this driver was more than 600 m beyond that ceiling. The fare ledger EV-FARE-02709 confirms SGD 4.50 was charged with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so that is the sum returned.\n\nThe rider's POL-NS-04 claims are rejected on their own test and are in any event unnecessary: the rider did message 'where are you? i dont see any car' at 07:39:15 and her device track (60 fixes, all within 13.8 m of the pin, inside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius) places her at the pickup, but the driver replied at 07:39:45, 30 seconds later, and POL-NS-04(b) requires that the driver not reply within 120 seconds. That clause therefore does not exonerate her; the refund rests instead on POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06, which do not depend on the rider's presence.\n\nThe driver's account ('I arrived and waited, the rider did not come') is contradicted by the trace, and POL-NS-12 does not assist him: the arrival marker here is a driver BUTTON press, not a platform GPS_AUTO confirmation, so POL-NS-12 is expressly inapplicable. No clause resolves an un-resolvable conflict, because POL-NS-05 resolves this one: the marker is false and the waiting clock cannot run from it, and with no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere the outcome under POL-NS-05(ii) is the same full refund.\n\nProfiles do not change anything. driver no_show_terminations_30d = 1 against completed_trips_30d = 103 (rate about 0.01) does not trip the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check (four or more AND above 0.08), and rider no_show_disputes_30d = 1 is below the POL-NS-09(d) threshold of 3; nothing escalates. The MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02709-01 (weight 0.0) carries no fact this ruling rests on — it only removes POL-NS-06(i)'s accumulation route, and there was no in-geofence interval to accumulate; the two claims resting on it were discarded for not disclosing its MISSING_ARTIFACT issue code.\n\nThe monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the SGD 8.00 POL-GEN-05 execution threshold and is executed automatically. Confidence is 0.95, capped by the weight 1.0 of the GPS trace that carries the deciding fact."
